    "Url": "https://github.com/kamaludu/bash4llm/",
    "Description": "Bash4LLM is a single-file Bash wrapper for interacting with LLMs from the terminal.  I created it because I wanted something simple that worked without installing Python, Node, or any other runtime.\u003Cp\u003EIt uses only Bash, curl, and jq. You can send prompts, start a small chat, process files line by line, stream output, and save session metadata in JSON format.\u003Cp\u003EI tried to make it safe and predictable: no use of the system \u0026#x2F;tmp, no use of eval. Groq is supported by default, and other provider",
